"""Tours: the battle between Poitiers and Tours, October 732.  A sample
game for the Grognard engine.

Abd al-Rahman al-Ghafiqi, governor of al-Andalus, has crossed the
Pyrenees, beaten Duke Odo of Aquitaine on the Garonne, sacked Bordeaux
and burnt the church outside Poitiers.  Now his horsemen ride north for
the abbey of Saint-Martin at Tours, and on the old Roman road between
the Clain and the Vienne they find Charles, mayor of the palace of the
Franks, waiting for them on a wooded rise, his men on foot in a solid
mass.  Play either side against the computer, or against a friend at
the same screen.

Run it with ./tours (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is saved
to ~/.tours.json.  ./tours --selftest checks the map and plays a game
between two computer players.
"""

